            <div xml:id="d239">

                <pb facs="0184" n="175" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg175"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/1617: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Glasgow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-11-20">November 20,
                        1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>79. Your 57, 18th.<anchor n="78" xml:id="d239-f1"/> Government unable at this
                    time to dispatch another vessel to British Isles to evacuate Americans due to
                    refusal of German Government to assure safe passage. In view of intent and
                    purpose of neutrality law to prevent travel in combat areas and increasing
                    perils of travel therein, Department declines authorize travel in such areas on
                    vessels of any character at this time.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
